This repository is generated from the Kestrix source tree (scripts/build_plugin_repo.py) and holds the
same plugin files that ship inside the kestrix-scan package on PyPI.

The fixing-security-findings skill is generated from the kestrix-scan rule registry. The rules were
written for Kestrix from their CWE entries and the language, library and standard documentation cited
per rule. No rule text, pattern or code from other scanners is included.

No advisory data is included. The install guard reads a local OSV index that the user builds with
`kestrix-scan db update` (https://osv.dev); its messages quote advisory ids and summaries from that
data, which OSV redistributes under each source's license (GitHub Advisory Database, PyPI Advisory
Database, OSS-Fuzz and EEF: CC-BY 4.0; OpenSSF Malicious Packages: Apache-2.0; Global Security
Database: CC0 1.0).
